  "body": "## Summary\n\n**Independent verification and audit, no new \u03ba.** This PR adds `research/t74-2751-joint-twelve-audit/`. It is a\nstandard-library, source-bound check of open PR #2751 (tekuuu, head `4cfbb0cc`; T74 joint twelve-lender recovery,\nconditional \u03ba \u2248 0.0017171416), with a computed reconciliation against open PR #2720 (petalas, head `813fae62`; \"Prove\nthe fixed-contract T74 inherited-correction floor\").\n\nInputs are 49 pinned git objects, read as data; no PR code is imported or run. **No defect was found.**\n\n**What it checks.** It corroborates and extends #2766's registered `independent_check.py`, the only independent check\nof PR2751 found so far:\n1. **PR2720, reproduced and reconciled.**\n   - PR2720's matrix reproduces on its own input words: det \u22121/16, together with its residual, continuation, forced\n     centres and invoice.\n   - On PR2751's words the same projection is zero. The partner correction moves to targets 21, 37, 47 and 110\n     (det 1/2), which no cut gate writes.\n   - PR2720's hypotheses are evaluated as computed booleans from verbatim quotes of its pinned README.\n     - **Changed:** h1 (h1a, h1b, h1c), the compensation clause of h2, h3, and the line-30 cut-frame premise.\n     - **Kept:** the continuation clause of h2, the cut incidences, the zero readers and the rank-8 producers.\n   - This independently confirms PR2751's own statement that it \"deliberately changes the old-four recovery paths\n     held fixed by PR2720\". PR2751 thereby answers PR2720's first open question constructively.\n2. **The change set and per-word delta** against PR2733@`2761b52b`: delta {1:\u22124, 7:\u22124, 8:+4} = 4(H8\u2212H7\u2212H1).\n3. **Words, lenders and pairs.**\n   - Both words are exact in the free-operator model through cleanup and the target endpoint, forward and dual.\n   - All 12 lenders hold their own input at both handoffs.\n   - All four pair recoveries `x += y/2; y \u2212= x` restore both sources from the exact pre-states.\n4. **Pricing.**\n   - The complete profile, from all 276,390 owner roles in two implementations.\n   - The complete delta 2664(H8\u2212H7\u2212H1) and stock 66,801.\n   - A rigorous enclosure that accepts C and rejects C + 1e-24.\n   - The comparison with PR2733's current head `a63c55ff`: a gap of 8.86e-7, not a dominance.\n5. **Downstream.**\n   - The four pairs, the line-45 partner charts and the twelve lifted targets are present in the words of #2802,\n     #2818, #2824, #2827 and #2833.\n   - #2766 and #2767 have identical complete profiles.\n\n**Controls.**\n- 356/356 negative controls are rejected (218 distinct), each by the rule it names, with 9 positive controls.\n- Mutation testing of the checker (local-only): 103 mutations, plus 7 new ones and a re-run sample. Every one fails.\n\n**Findings for the authors (non-blocking).**\n- PR2751's PROOF.md calls the recovery gates \"added\", but against PR2696 and PR2733 they are moved.\n- PR2751's ops 47\u201350 keep their ids with new charts.\n- #2767's top-level `PROFILE.json` and some README lines carry earlier profiles.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2751-joint-twelve-audit/verify.py --fetch\n```\n\nIt takes about 3 min and about 1.0 GB, and needs git \u2265 2.29 and network access for `--fetch`. The expected final line\nis in the README; it ends `negative_controls=356/356-rejected distinct_controls=218 positive_controls=9 pinned_inputs=49`.\n`--check-only` gives `PASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS`, and the repo helper tests (`test_research_*`) pass. The\nregistered command has been run only on CPython 3.14.4, not on Python 3.12.\n\n## Scope, task and overlap\n\n- **Card:** `independent-moment` (independent-verification), refined. The loop drew seed 63 (adversarial-audit track).\n- **Priority revision:** 5.\n- **Base:** `4cc9d09a`.\n- **Milestone:** audit.\n- **Family expansion decision:** none.\n- **Canonical thread:** Discussion #2612.\n\n**Not re-derived (author-checked):**\n- the native identity of the K47\u2013K50 charts (PR2751's own warp checks and #2768 cover this author-side);\n- strict supplier admission and the 63 outer inequalities;\n- two unevaluated PR2720 cut-bill premises.\n\n**Overlap** (refreshed 2026-10-16 05:12 UTC):\n- #2766's `independent_check.py` and #2768 are described head by head in the README.\n- PR2847, from a separate session of this account, audits #2802's increment and is complementary.\n- Main's ledger records #2751 and #2720 as partially reviewed, with maintainer review in progress.\n- The selected frontier is unchanged (\u03ba = 0.001672660197076918, #1094).\n\n## Credits and disclosure\n\n- **Audited:** tekuuu (#2751), petalas (#2720).\n- **Predecessors:** mason-hale (#2696), tekuuu (#2436), zxv (#2530), philippeVV (#2679), jeremykothe2 (#2462, #2588,\n  #2673, #2745, #2269), mdumitrean (#2733), Cinna Davis (#2226).\n- **Related:** DavidAriasC (#2766), jeremykothe2 (#2767), Dugongue (#2824, #2827).\n- **Conflicts:** both audited PRs' retained notices credit this author's PR1964 in the inherited lineage. This package\n  reuses this author's own earlier checkers (#2315, #2387, #2804).\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5): AI scouts, three\nindependent AI auditors, AI builders and two rounds of AI review. No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
